>full maximum strength?  "3 blessed potions of gain ability" is a good wish,
>but I wouldn't start wishing for such "luxuries" until I had the essentials:
>
>blessed +3 war hammer named Mjollnir
>blessed +3 gray dragon scale mail
>blessed amulet of life saving
>blessed +3 shield of reflection
>blessed +3 pair of gauntlets of power
>blessed +3 speed boots
>
>Nice things like luckstones and potions of gain ability are easy to get
>by polymorphing junk, but the above items are too rare.
gauntlets of power and speed boots are very easy to make with polymorphing.
An amulet of life saving is luxury (it takes also lots of food). Besides,
it only delays termination of your character, if you are so stupid to die, you
will probably also on the next level (not true in nethack 2.3).

I agree that a good weapon and good armor is most important, however if I get
a wish on level 20 or more and I have nothing to enter the castle I always
wish for a blessed ring of levitation (also for the Elbereth/levitation trick).
An Ac of -10 is enough to reach the castle and it's easier to attack the castle
with an Ac of -10 and a ring of conflict than with an Ac of -20 and without
a ring of conflict. If you are not lawful it can be wise to wish for a
helm of oposite alignment (especially if you have a wand of polymorph, you
can polymorph scrolls to enchant weapon and enchant armor and chest to
magic lamps and bless them with holy water from the lawful altar).

So a wish depends on your situation (I have wished for a floating eye
corpse, nobody on the news mentioned that).

